From 3f33313a57a54a76f93eaa62e542743b9a184365 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 04:50:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 211/217] feat: volumetric fog on the ray traced reflected
 segment (decision 09 section 9.3)

A reflection now picks up the same froxel fog the direct view does, instead of only
the analytic global fog.

The source is CVolumetricFogStage's LOCAL froxel volume (the raymarch input, after
temporal reprojection), read from the PREVIOUS frame. That is not a compromise: the
stage runs at StandardGraphicsPipeline.cpp:536, after CSceneForwardStage::ExecuteOpaque
at :523, so CE's own forward shading already samples a one-frame-old froxel volume.
Reading it from the SVO block at :460 therefore needs no pipeline reordering at all
and the stock frame order is untouched.

Not the accumulated volume (s_ptexVolumetricFog / GetVolumetricFogTex): it holds
in-scatter accumulated FROM THE CAMERA, so the endpoint difference fog(hit) - fog(surface)
is only valid when both endpoints sit on one camera ray. A mirror on a back wall
reflecting something in front of it puts the hit nearer the camera than the surface,
the difference goes negative and the reflection gets no fog - the most common mirror
shot there is. The local volume's two fields are per-unit-length in-scattered radiance
and extinction, so they integrate along any direction.

ShadePS marches the segment surface -> hit with 8 steps using CE's own integrator
(VolumeLighting.cfi RaymarchVolumetricFogCS, unchanged), projecting each sample point
with SVO_ViewProj to get the froxel texcoord. Steps that land off screen, behind the
near plane or past farDistCenter have no froxel data; they are counted and the analytic
global fog covers their share of the segment as T_analytic ^ (1 - covered). With no
coverage that collapses to the exact lerp this pass has always done, so r_VolumetricFog 0
falls back cleanly.

Only the reflected segment is added. The camera -> surface segment is fogged downstream
by CFogStage / CVolumetricFogStage on the composited image; adding it here would count
it twice. A miss is still not fogged - the sky and the probes carry their own aerial
perspective.

Exposure: the froxel volume is injected from a scattering colour the CPU pre-multiplies
by GetSceneReferredExposure() (VolumetricFog.cpp:2513) and from pre-exposed tiled lights,
so its in-scatter is EXPOSED radiance, the same units GetVolumetricFogColorInternal's own
PS_HDR_RANGE_ADAPT_MAX multiply produces. Both go in before ShadePS's single divide.
The transmittances are unit free.

Debug view 18 = the in-scatter added at the hit; 19 = the transmittance of the reflected
segment, tinted green where the froxels covered it and red where the analytic fog did.

Bindings: SVO_VolFogInscatter t41, SVO_VolFogDensity t50 (the density has its own R16F
volume when r_HDRTexFormat 0 makes the in-scatter volume R11G11B10F, which has no alpha),
SVO_VolFogParams, and SVO_ViewProj, which is no longer debug-only. VolumetricFog.h gains
four const accessors and no behaviour.

All shader hunks are inside %_RT_QUALITY; all C++ is behind e_svoTI_RT_Active. cryfx_lint
0 findings, rtharness2 17 compiles 0 errors, CryRenderD3D11 Profile 0 errors 0 warnings.

